                <pb facs="0768" n="683" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg683"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">819.51/156: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Panama</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Price</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Panama</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-10-28T16:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 28,
                                1918, 4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received 7.43
                            p.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Panama President writes me that “the arrival of the financial expert that we
                    urgently need and which has been suggested or recommended by the State
                    Department is anxiously awaited,” to [which I] have replied that I understood
                    that his coming would follow the [passage] of such law by Panama as would enable
                    him to render satisfactory service. While [waiting] upon such suggested law I
                    suggest that steps be taken to locate such expert that he may come as promptly
                    as possible following passage of law. Panama President to-day asks prompt
                    response to the question of appointment of General Guardia as Secretary of the
                    Treasury submitted by my cablegram of October 25th 4 p.m.<anchor n="5"
                        xml:id="d651-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Price</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
